the town hall in paris 15th district  a new batch of covid vaccines arrives  inside a doctor measures out doses ready  for use  elderly people are being prioritized for  immunization  those here are hopeful that life may  soon return to normal  i'm just desperate to do things again i  feel like i've been stagnating  and i couldn't wait to have this vaccine  the goal is that everyone is vaccinated  as fast as possible so the virus recedes  as the number of people vaccinated  against covid in france grows  so does talk of a vaccine passport to  travel  this french politician says such a  document could also be used to visit  restaurants or theaters  those who are vaccinated should be able  to resume activities  the vaccination passport would show that  a person is no longer in danger  themselves and no longer a danger to  others  supporters of a vaccine passport say  could help revive  vital economic sectors like tourism  paris  is usually one of the world's most  visited cities but  in the past year few people have come to  admire its monuments  or enjoy attractions like this cruise  the owner of this boat tour company  on the river sends says he would welcome  a vaccine passport  it would encourage international  travelers to return to the city because  without them  it will be a challenge to keep the  business afloat  any solutions that can help us live  normally again would be good  there are already countries that require  vaccinations to enter  so a vaccine passport is a good idea if  it can help  everyone work again opinion polls  suggest that a majority of people in  france support  a vaccine passport for travel or access  to certain services  but the french government says it's far  too early to consider such a measure  that it would be divisive because not  enough people have been immunized  and many don't wish to be it would be  unfair and especially in france where we  have you know this uh  we are very well attached to the  equality principles so  exactly it could be the reaction could  be okay  only the first people to be vaccinated  will have those rights  and not ourselves none and we have to  queue we have to wait for a while before  getting vaccinated so it's unfair eu  leaders will discuss the idea of a  vaccine passport during a meeting  thursday the issue divides member states  it's clear though that opening up  economies and offering some freedoms  won't be easy  while the eu's still navigating its  worst ever health emergency  natasha butler al jazeera paris
 

